<title>USA: U.S. rice weekly export sales highlights--USDA.</title>
<headline>U.S. rice weekly export sales highlights--USDA.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-10-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. rice major sales activity in the week ended Oct 17 reported by exporters for the following purchasing countries, in tonnes:</p>
<p>Net Sales:	1996/97		 1997/98</p>
<p> Nicaragua	10,500-A		 Nil</p>
<p> Mexico	    6,200-B</p>
<p> El Salvador     4,500-C</p>
<p> L &amp; W'ward Isls 2,800</p>
<p> Honduras	  2,600</p>
<p> Canada	    2,200</p>
<p>A-includes 8,500 rough rice.</p>
<p>B-includes 5,800 rough.</p>
<p>C-all rough.</p>
<p>Net sales of 33,800 tonnes were 18 percent above the previous week but 43 percent below the four-week average.</p>
<p>Exports of 26,800 tonnes were 18 percent below the previous week and 45 percent under the four-week average.</p>
<p>Primary export destinations: Saudi Arabia (11,100), Jamaica (5,000, Mexico (4,600), Nicaragua (2,100) and Britain (1,400).</p>
